WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:05.968
Celine: What are you doing?

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.220
Detective: Who the hell are you?

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.475
Colonel: Celine? What are you doing here?

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.100
Detective: "Celine"? How the hell do you know her?

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.140
Butler: Madame, I'm afraid you've come at a very inopportune time. Something dreadful has happened here.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.080
Celine: I can see that, and I'm glad I got here before it got any worse.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.440
Chef: This is only the tip of the iceberg! And it's a big iceberg.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.260
Chef: How can I put this delicately?

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.180
Chef: MARK'S FUCKING DEAD!

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:26.840
Celine: What?

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.420
Chef: Dead, like my hopes and dreams.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.220
Chef: And he's a flesh-eating zombie, too.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.400
Celine: Homo necrosis.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.140
Colonel: Exactly, hence the guns.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.800
Detective: That is not "hence the guns"!

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.900
Butler: Stop waving those bloody guns around!

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.580
Celine: Hol-hold on! Tell me what happened! How did Mark...die?

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.200
Mayor (offscreen): It was murder.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.900
And worse yet...

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.820
The body is missing.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.860
Celine: What? Show me. And don't say that word.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.300
Chef:  What word? Murder?

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.720
Celine: Yes! That word!

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.960
Butler:  Well, I mean murder is a rather accurate description of what occur—

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.960
Celine: Do you not see the lightning?

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.660
Detective: You sayin' it was lightning that murdered Mark?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.820
Colonel: Well, Mother Nature doesn't exactly strike me as having murderous intent.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.540
...Unless you count that time I was sucked into the board game: Jumanji and I wa—!

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:19.280
Celine: Stop, stop! Look, whatever's happening here is tapping into forces far beyond our control.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.440
Chef (quietly): murder.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.060
Colonel (slowly): Mur...doch?

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.300
Detective: Malarkey.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.460
Butler: Marco!
[The thunder proceeds to be done with them messing around] 
Celine: Enough!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:47.340
Look. Mark's death is a terrible thing indeed. But I fear that there are forces much darker than anything we've seen here today.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:54.880
I'm well versed in the arcane arts, but if you, untrained and uninitiated, can summon lightning with a mere word,

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.260
we're all in far graver danger than anything we could ever hope to face alone.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.800
We're gonna have to work together if we're gonna survive this.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.180
Mayor:  Celine, what are you proposing?

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.000
Celine: We need to speak with Mark.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.120
Chef: I knew it! He's a flesh-eating zombie!
Celine: No.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.100
Colonel:  Well, maybe one of those smart zombies: homeo sapio zombifus.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.160
Celine:  No, no. I need to commune with the dead.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.640
Detective: That... doesn't sound like a good idea.
Celine: Well, it's a good thing I don't need your permission.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.700
Celine: But you! You've been awfully quiet through this whole thing.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.700
Chef: With those beady little eyes.
Butler: And wearing THOSE rags, pff.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.860
Detective: Maybe I shouldn't have trusted someone so goddamn gorgeous.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.580
Colonel: Oh, I'll pass.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:45.080
Celine: But I feel like I can trust you. I sense that you have a far greater part to play in all of this.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.740
Will you help me find an answer?

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.800
Perfect. Come with me.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.780
Detective: Alright, that's enough. I'm not gonna just sit around and let you drag my partner off to their very likely death. I won't stand for it!

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.700
Colonel: Well, I trust Celine with all my heart! I see no reason why an-any-any one should doubt her!

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:08.060
Butler:  Well, I have to agree with our intrepid detective here. It just doesn't seem natural.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.060
Chef: I never liked this uptight asshole. He walks around with a stick up his ass.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.760
But I think he's right, something's weird.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:22.020
Celine: If it makes you feel any better, you guys can stand watch outside the door, but my work CANNOT be interrupted.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:27.340
Detective: Oh, believe you me. I'll be keeping a close eye on every single one of you.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.100
Even myself.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.560
Especially myself.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:39.560
Mayor: Wh—Celine? Celine, wait. Wait!
Celine: Yes, Damien?

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.440
Damien: I... are you alright?

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.060
Celine: (sighs) Damien: I know this news can't be settling well with you.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.700
Celine: I'm fine for now.
Damien: I... er...

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:52.640
But all this talk of the occult! And—and Mark is dead, wait! Wait.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.080
I just didn't think you were the type to become mixed up with all this.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:04.200
Celine: There is more to this world than you could ever hope to imagine. I just had my eyes open to a small portion of it.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.420
Damien:  I... [Sigh]

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.300
Just be careful!

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:11.200
You too.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.300
Celine: Could you hand me my bag?

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.980
Thank you. Please, have a seat.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.520
Now, I'm sure this must be unsettling for you, being thrust into this series of unfortunate events.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.700
But I promise—with your help, I'm going to get to the bottom of this.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:52.540
Now I'm not sure who would want to kill Mark, but something tells me this seemingly significant event

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:56.960
is actually a footnote in a much larger mystery unfolding in our midst.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.980
I've never been very comfortable in this house. 
But something tells me...

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:08.760
Now that my eyes are open, there are dark forces surrounding this manor.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.120
(Audio slows, distorts. Speech fades in and out)
Detective:  Keep your enemies close, eh?

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:19.900
Colonel: I will not be called a murderer in my own home!
Celine: Stop!

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:28.640
Colonel: I thought it was time that we come get to know each other, far away from the prying eyes of...anyone else.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.120
Detective: You're not gonna believe this. I can't believe this. The body—the body is gone. It's fucking gone!

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:34.940
[Piercing ring begins to penetrate muddled noise]

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:42.660
Damien:  ...Not exactly sure what we're supposed to be celebrating. I mean, it's good to have the gang back together, but out of the blue like this seems..

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:50.760
(???, laughing) Employers come and go, come and go. Some die, some don't.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.620
(Thunderclap, audio returns to normal)
Celine: What happened? Why did you stop?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.220
Did you see something? Someone? Draw it.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.900
What is this? This doesn't answer anything!

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.240
You need to go back! Go back, now!

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.660
Detective: What the shit is this?

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.840
Celine: Get out! We are not done here!
Mayor: Celine, I think this is quite enough.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.180
Celine:  It's enough when I SAY it's enough!
Detective:  C'mon, partner, let's go. Come on! Hurry it up!

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.260
What did she do to you? What is this? Butler! Butler!

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.520
Butler: What? What is it?
Detective: This mean anything to you?

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:33.800
Butler: Well, maybe...no, sorry.
Detective: Spit it out if you got something!

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:38.360
Butler: Well...it could be our groundskeeper George, but he only works on weekdays.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:41.340
Detective: Looks like your friend here may disagree with that notion!

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.900
Chef: Me?
Detective: Yeah, you.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:50.960
Chef:  Uh...I don't know shit, I plead the fifth, man.
Butler: Chef, if you know something, for god's sake spit it out!

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:58.480
Chef: Okay, alright, you're twisting my arm, alright. George has been living on the grounds for years.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.340
Butler: WHAT?!
Detective: And you just now thought to share that information with us?

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:04.740
For all we know, he could be the murderer!

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:08.160
Celine: For the last time, stop saying that word!

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:14.320
Chef: Look. George... just tends to the grounds, man. He's a fuckin' hermit!

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.800
Detective: I don't care what the fuck he is!

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:21.880
Mayor: Look, all this arguing is getting us nowhere! Just go outside and talk to this George and be done with it!

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:26.960
Detective: Hold on a sec. You're not coming with us?
Mayor: I-I need to stay here with Celine.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.800
Celine: I don't need help. Especially from you!
Mayor: OUR FRIEND IS DEAD!

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:42.880
I'm sorry. I just need answers to all of this. I already lost one friend today; I don't want to lose another.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.700
Celine: Fine, but I need to stay here.
Mayor: Fine with me.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:52.260
Detective: Fine, good, yeah, whatever, who cares. Alright, you're coming with me. Partner, you too.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.180
Hold on a sec... We're missing somebody.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:00.000
Who had eyes on the Colonel?
Butler: Well, he appeared tired, and...went back to his room.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.660
Detective: I'm sure he did. And with any luck, he'll stay there. Alright, let's roll out. Come on.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.780
Detective (offscreen):  Move it. Come on, partner, come on!

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.360
Detective:  Lead the way, Cookie.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:16.500
Chef: Cookie? I'm not your Cookie! I spent three weeks at culinary school! I earned the right to be called a chef!

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.680
Detective: I'm very impressed. Just tell us where we're going!

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.400
Come on! Let's go!

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.740
Detective: I think I see him.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:36.600
Hey! Buddy! Hands where I can see 'em!

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.280
George: Hey, my hands are where they're supposed to be. Unless, of course, you'd like to dig the hole for yourself.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:47.320
Detective: What the hell are you doing here?
George: I'm the groundskeeper. I keep the ground, alright?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:52.080
I'd say look around. The ground is pretty well kept in this place, right?

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.940
Chef: I'm sorry, man, this dick made me bring him out here.
Detective: You shut up.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.380
How do you not know about the murders going on in this house? (Interrupted by thunder)

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.100
How do you not hear that lightning?

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:07.500
George: Lightning is the sky's business! Look at the ground! When the ground starts shooting up lightning, I'll let you know!

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:14.520
Detective: Alright then, smartass, why exactly are you digging that hole? And why shouldn't we suspect you for taking part in the death of your employer?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:22.160
George: (laughs) Employers come and go! Some die, some don't, some are murdered, some are not. It's not my business!

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.020
I'm digging this hole for a burst water pipe, if that's alright with your gracefulness!

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:32.400
Chef: See, I told you. George didn't do nothin, man!
George: See? I just did nothing.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.500
Detective: Forgive me for not taking you at face value.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:39.760
But we're all gonna come inside, we're gonna sit down, and have a nice lovely chat.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.440
And get to the bottom of this before I lose my mind, and start dabbling in murder myself!

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:56.160
George: Now, you listen to me, sonny. It's been fifteen years since I've been in that house. And I am not about to break that winning streak now.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:04.520
I don't care how many murders there've been. I ain't going near that house!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:17.180
However, there is one reason. One incident. One manifestation. That will get me into that mad house.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:27.820
You had better pray to God that that reason never comes to pass.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.120
(thunderclap)

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.640
THAT THERE'S THE REASON!

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.760
Detective: Go, go, go!

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.760
(Dramatic music) George: Somebody help me!

